ant to play a geography quiz  whatever those invocation phrases are  they all get translated to a same thing  which is play a quiz and then your app  could be one of these apps that  participates in that auction based on  how it has done in the past and  personalized results for the user we  show a carousel of few apps that can  have been that auction and a user can  play and play with any of these so think  of this and these are very like I talked  about earlier like if you are in the  meditation space you are in the coffee  ordering space you are in health care  space a banking space like this is we  have built in intents for a lot of these  and you can sign up for any of those the  third pillar that we have for discovery  is what we call action links action  links are a link to your action or to  your app so they are pretty much like  your website URL or a deep link into  your Android app and so on so once you  create an action link you can actually  use it just like your URL in any kind of  any kind of surface so you can use it in  your websites you can use it in your  apps you can use it on social platforms  you can use it in your marketing  campaigns like in your emails and so on  you can even use it on billboards if you  want the idea really is this is how you  tell users that I have one more surface  which is more optimized for some  specific use cases but you can actually  engage with that surface so it's  important to think on those lines again  as I said it's fairly easy to create an  action link when you go to dialogue flow  there is a section in there which would  actually give you a link for each of  your actions you can create separate  ones for different intents that your  action supports so if you do multiple  things like I want to track my order  there could be a separate link versus I  want to place an order there a separate  link I want to reorder something there  could be a separate link and so on now I  talked about discovery quite a bit one  of the big things that a lot of  developers are interested in is how do i  monetize my experience how do I kind of  make once I start driving traffic to it  and start  putting money behind this assistant app  how do I start monetizing it so today we  support physical goods and transaction  sales on the platform  we are live in seven different markets  US UK Canada Australia Germany Japan and  France so and we are rolling out in many  more markets to the rest of the year our  plan is for this map to look a lot more  green by the end of the year and we are  launching multiple markets every month  and when we talk about transactions  these are transactions about physical  goods and services but these are also  things like you want to book a table  book or take our test drive and  reservations if you think or a makeover  appointment and so on so transaction  flows are fairly standard like if you  think of the building blocks and we  support all of these building blocks  today you can customize it based on your  needs and so on but the three steps for  most part the first one is you build the  order or build a cart kind of thing this  is where you figure out what's the plot  a user wants to buy you upsell  cross-sell other things  what's the reservation the user wants  what time works for them and things like  that so think on those lines but the  first step is you build an order once  you build an order you propose the order  to the user is that are you able to  confirm or this is the right payment  method you are using and so on so you  confirm the order the transaction goes  through the third piece is very  important when it comes to an assistant  surface it sent updates on the order we  have API is where you can push in  updates on the order so if it's a  reservation your reservation has been  confirmed or your table is now ready or  sorry we had to push out the reservation  by half an hour and things like that if  it's a transaction things like your  package has been shaped or it's arrived  and so on are important to send to the  user more proactively we support  multiple helpers to make it easy for our  developers to build transactions there's  a location helper if you want the  current location the user we have  address helpers if you want that really  delivery address of the user we have  payment helpers where we can actually  help with payment instruments Google has  on file for users  we have payment credentials for hundreds  of millions of users through our Google  Play a Google pay offering and you can  use those helpers matt talked about you  also have account linking helpers  to make it easy for you to link account  with Google users we are also piloting  digital goods digital goods are also  another way developers can monetize  their experiences so when I talk about  digital goods think of in-app digital  goods like if you're in the gaming  industry you can sell coins and gems and  extra lives turns play time and things  like that and that's a fairly big  business when it comes to digital goods  we also now support subscription  services which is if you're in the  premium content space like news or  premium subscriptions premium services  this is one way to monetize your  experience which is through  subscriptions or music for that matter  and then the third thing is digital  assets like a digital book or a movies  and stuff like that you can sell that on  the platform too and that's other  digital goods that we support  so across physical goods services  reservations digital goods we have a  good portfolio of ways our developers  can come in and create transactional  experiences on assistent when you  actually figure out the right use case  that works for users an assistant  surfaces this is something that helps  you monetize those experiences for your  users and then the last piece I'll talk  about is how do you drive reengagement  for users you have loyal customers or  you have customers you've tried your  experience once how do you bring them  back and what are the platform  constructs we support so you can bring  users back into your experience is the  same side I had earlier on is we have  touch points with users throughout the  day and we offer channels to developers  so that they can reach back to their  users at different points of this  journey so if you if you are a use case  where which you want more and more users  to engage in the morning like we have  different ways you can actually get  become part of that habit for users or  throughout the day or through the  evening routine and so on so let me talk  about an example of that we have  something that we call routines we have  lot of default routines that we have  created for users routines is nothing  but it is multiple actions bundled to a  single command so from a user's  perspective let's say user says good  morning or hey Google good morning it it  kicks off a series of actions for the  user so it can turn off their heat it  can move their phone out of the silent  mode it tells the user about the top  news their stock portfolio updates it  tells about their calendar how their  commute is going to be for to work and  so on and a user can configure it set it  up and so on but that's just one example  of a routine and you as a developer  could has a way to to get become part of  the routines like a tip of the day or  the thought of the day or how long is  the wait line at at Caltrain and things  like that so this is one way where you  can proactively be part of users  journeys or your action can be a  proactive part of user journeys and then  many more that we have out there we this  is a big engagement point for users  today where we see users using these  routines a lot because it helps them  make certain part of the day a lot more  seamless and efficient a fairly easy way  for you as a developer to sign up for  intense or for any of these routines if  you go to the console it's an opt-in you  sign up saying I want my action to be  eligible for any of these routines and  you turn on that radio button and your  your option shows up to users to be part  of that routine there are couple of  other ways that we support to drive  reengagement the first one is daily  updates the thing with daily updates is  that these are the updates that Google  sends to the user saying we think this  is a relevant experience for you or this  is the relevant call to action for you  we work with developers to figure out  what are the right ones to send to the  user and that's one way where we can be  proactive the second piece is push  notifications this is a like the push  notifications you have on the app  ecosystem  users opt into getting push  notifications from you like the example  from a square here and users will  proactively see every time you want to  push an update so this could be an  update in terms of there is a new  product available or you signed up for a  certain deal that's available or a deal  of the day or whatever it is so you can  think of what is relevant for your  business  but you can start pushing out  notifications to the user through  various google surfaces not just on the  assistant site so that's all that I had  in terms of how do you drive  reengagement for your users we have a  lot of assets and resources out there  that you can use to learn more about  this we have best practices on design  how to create the right design examples  that you want to sell tickets we have  examples on how you do that you want to  create games your examples on how to  create that and for different parts of  the different verticals we have a lot of  example code example designs that you  can use and then you can sign up for a  mailing list to stay updated with all  the new and upcoming launches I think  that's all we had and thank you for so  much for your time  you

